media/gpu/v4l2: encode mapped frames through MMAP input buffers

V4L2VideoEncodeAccelerator queues shared-memory frames as USERPTR
buffers. Encoders that read their input through an IOMMU of their own
often offer only MMAP and DMABUF on the input queue (the Apple AVE does),
and there every shared-memory encode fails at the first QBUF.

Ask the input queue which memory types it takes (VIDIOC_REQBUFS
capabilities). Where USERPTR is not among them, allocate MMAP input
buffers and copy each color plane of the frame into the buffer at the
device's plane offset and stride. Drivers that take USERPTR, and every
DMABUF path, are unchanged.

--- a/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_encode_accelerator.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_encode_accelerator.cc
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 
 #include "media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_encode_accelerator.h"
 
+#include <algorithm>
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <linux/videodev2.h>
 #include <poll.h>
